'''Death Aura''' is a [[spell]] that grants an [[aura]] that deals [[Chaos damage|chaos]] [[damage over time]] around the user, like {{il|Righteous Fire}}. It is granted by {{il|Death's Oath}}.

==Mechanics==
Death Aura is a [[trigger]]ed skill that's always active while you have the item that grants the skill equipped. 

Death Aura's damage affected by modifiers to [[aura]] effect, [[damage over time]], [[damage over time multiplier]], and [[chaos damage]], but ''not'' area damage. The tooltip damage does not display damage increases from {{c|magic|X% increased effect of Non-Curse Auras you Cast}} modifier, but the actual damage of the skill is affected by these modifiers.<ref name = "aura_mods" />

The base radius of Death Aura is 3 metres (30 units).{{citation needed}}

Currently, there are several support gems that affect Death Aura beneficially:
* {{il|Concentrated Effect Support}}
* {{il|Increased Area of Effect Support}}
* {{il|Efficacy Support}}
* {{il|Arrogance Support}} ({{c|mod|Supported Skills have (10-19)% increased Aura effect}} gem mod only; despite tooltip dps would not reflect it<ref name = "aura_mods" /> )
* {{il|Void Manipulation Support}}
* {{il|Item Rarity Support}}
* {{il|Item Quantity Support}} (currently unobtainable normally)

Since '''Death Aura''' is a [[trigger]]ed skill, it will ''not'' be activated if equipped on {{il|Animate Guardian}}. The on-kill damage taken, however, still applies.

===Lifetap Support===
{{il|Lifetap Support}} can add duration mod to the skill so that it can be supported by 
* {{il|Swift Affliction Support}}<ref name=ArcaneSurge315/>
* {{il|Less Duration Support}} ({{c|mod|Supported Skills deal #% more Damage}} gem mod only; not affected by other mod of the gem)

While the Lifetap Support gem itself requires a secondary skill supported by Lifetap and spent life to gain {{stl|Lifetap}} buff in order to trigger the gem mod {{c|mod|Supported Skills deal #% more Damage while you have Lifetap}}; Death Aura itself does not gain the {{stl|Lifetap}} buff as the Aura does not cost mana or life.

===Other Considerations===
* {{il|Despair}} linked to {{il|Blasphemy Support}} or {{il|Witchfire Brew}} to curse nearby enemies
* [[Occultist]]'s [[Profane Bloom]] or another [[explode|on-death explosion effect]] can kill packs of monsters sooner
* [[Withered]] increases the chaos damage taken by enemies and can be applied automatically by [[Occultist]]'s [[Withering Presence]]
* The mod on {{il|Death's Oath}} {{c|mod|You take 450 Chaos Damage per second for 3 seconds on Kill}} can be countered with life regeneration and chaos resistance. For example, at 75% chaos resistance, 112.5 life regeneration per second is needed. [[Chaos Inoculation]] is not recommended as [[Death's Oath]] does not have any [[energy shield]].
* {{il|Tainted Pact}} converts the chaos damage over time to healing over time, while leeching
* {{il|The Sundered Will}} can raise Death Aura's damage even further by scaling increased chaos damage.
* Death's Oath can be used to create a [[Vestigial unique item]] that grants Death Aura, which lets you gain access to the skill while not having to deal with the chaos damage degen from the armour itself while potentially being on a unique body armour with stats more suited for the north side of the passive tree.

==Drop restrictions==
Death Aura can only be obtained from {{il|Death's Oath}}.

